OL,3,AHusband calls for PM to intervene after
OL,4,Awife detained in Egypt
OL,5,
OL,6,FThe husband of a woman who was detained
OL,7,Fby the Egyptian authorities has called
OL,8,Ffor Prime Minister Andy Burnham to get
OL,9,Finvolved and help with her release.
OL,11,FEman el-Shazly, from Handsworth Wood,
OL,12,Fin Birmingham, was taken from her
OL,13,Fmother's house in Cairo two months ago,
OL,14,Fallegedly in relation to her sister's
OL,15,Fonline activism.
OL,17,FHer husband, Zeesharn Moustapha, said
OL,18,Fthat their family felt "very helpless"
OL,19,Fand that their "only possible solution"
OL,20,Fwas for Burnham to "make a phone call
OL,21,Fto Egypt" to end the detainment.
OL,23,APub: 17-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
